01:15:41.710 --> 01:15:45.430
OK, so in general, we saw that
we got this hexagonal lattice

01:15:45.430 --> 01:15:46.720
we had to work out the maths.

01:15:46.720 --> 01:15:48.220
We actually didn't
show the maths,

01:15:48.220 --> 01:15:50.230
but you can look at the notes.

01:15:50.230 --> 01:15:52.480
Or even before, we had
to really figure out

01:15:52.480 --> 01:15:55.180
what's the optimal value.

01:15:55.180 --> 01:15:58.210
And it's kind of
obvious, as we are

01:15:58.210 --> 01:16:02.980
working through this, that your
quantize value and decision

01:16:02.980 --> 01:16:05.560
regions are intertwined.

01:16:05.560 --> 01:16:08.200
The quantize value will
depend on the decision region,

01:16:08.200 --> 01:16:09.760
and the decision
region will depend

01:16:09.760 --> 01:16:12.250
on the nearby quantize values.

01:16:12.250 --> 01:16:16.610
And these things are
really hard to compute.

01:16:16.610 --> 01:16:19.490
And so one way to
resolve this in practice

01:16:19.490 --> 01:16:22.430
is we can do some sort of
an iterative algorithm.

01:16:24.950 --> 01:16:26.960
Before I move on, have
